            "bookkeeping": "The informal normalization makes $T(\\omega)=\\omega$ for loops at $x$. Lean proves $\\tau_x\\in H$ and uses closure under multiplication and inverses to recover the original loop.",
            "conclusion": "Here we choose $\\tau_x=1$; TauCeti keeps $\\tau_x$ arbitrary and cancels it.",
            "declaration": "iSup_range_map_subtypeVal_eq_top",
            "lines": [126, 179]
          },
          "snippet": {
            "line": 169,
            "text": "  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun γ _ ↦ ?_\n  have hγ : γ.asHom ∈ S.arrows (mk x) (mk x) := by\n    rw [hS]\n    trivial\n  have hτx : (End.of (τ (mk x)) : _root_.FundamentalGroup X x) ∈ H :=\n    fromPath_mem_iSup_range hx _ (hτ' x)\n  have h := H.mul_mem hτx (H.mul_mem hγ (H.inv_mem hτx))\n  rw [hinv] at h\n  convert h using 1\n  ext\n  simp"
          }
